From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rui Figueira <rfigueira@cloudflare.com>
Date: Tue, 15 Sep 2026 21:19:03 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Enable container queries, cq units and anchor parsing in
 servo
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

cq* units were gecko-gated at tokenization, so any calc() containing
them failed to parse in the servo build. WPT's sign(2cqw - 10px) probes
across css-color, css-flexbox, css-fonts, css-lists and css-grid hit
this. The container-size-query plumbing itself is feature-agnostic and
falls back to the small viewport when there is no container, so only the
parse gate needs to go.

Servo already compiles the anchor value implementations, but preference
checks reject every anchor() and anchor-size() value. The remaining
checks are crate::pref!("layout.css.anchor-positioning.enabled", gecko =
true), which is off by default in servo. Ship the parser support
unconditionally and generate the remaining anchor properties for Servo.

The @container rule and the container shorthand were gated to the gecko
build, so the servo build rejected them at parse time. Drop the gates.
The shorthand serializes its container-type only when that longhand is
present and not normal.

Co-authored-by: Luís Duarte <lduarte@cloudflare.com>
Co-authored-by: bpereira <bpereira@cloudflare.com>
